export default {"id":"m4l-level-19","number":19,"title":"Capstone","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"p","modules":[{"id":"m4l-m-1-1","code":"1","title":"p","blurb":"p","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"m4l-l-p","title":"Project: Production Max for Live Device Suite","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Project Overview and Scope","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Track:</strong> <code>m4l-devices</code>","<strong>Deliverable:</strong> A complete, commercial-grade, multi-device <strong>Max for Live Production Suite</strong> comprising 3 to 5 fully realized <code>.amxd</code> devices, accompanying native presets (<code>.adv</code>), a demonstration Live Set (<code>.als</code>), and comprehensive documentation (<code>README.md</code>).","<strong>Target Studio:</strong> Ableton Live 12 Standard (with Max for Live add-on) / Live 12 Suite; bundled Cycling '74 Max 9 runtime.","<strong>Cross-Platform Target:</strong> Windows 10/11 (64-bit) and macOS 12+ (Universal Binary / Apple Silicon &amp; Intel).","<strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Successful completion of all progress gates (Gates A through L, Lessons 1.1.1–17.5.1)."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"2. Technical Suite Requirements","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                        CAPSTONE SUITE ARCHITECTURE MATRIX                         |\n+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+\n| Specification     | Mandatory Technical Requirement                               |\n+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Device Count**  | **3 to 5 discrete `.amxd` devices** unified by a coherent     |\n|                   | musical or workflow design concept (e.g., Analog Studio Suite,|\n|                   | Ambient Generative Toolkit, Live Performance Utility Rack).   |\n+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Device Family   | Must include devices from at least **TWO distinct families**: |\n| Diversity**       | 1. Max Audio Effect                                           |\n|                   | 2. Max MIDI Effect                                            |\n|                   | 3. Max Instrument                                             |\n|                   | 4. Live 12 MIDI Tool (Transformation or Generator)            |\n|                   | 5. Live API Session Utility                                   |\n+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Parameter       | - 100% compliance with Long Name immutability &amp; uniqueness.   |\n| Hygiene**         | - Type &amp; Unit Styles explicitly declared across all controls. |\n|                   | - Clip Modulation Modes set (Bipolar for continuous floats).  |\n|                   | - Initial Enable &amp; Initial Values configured for factory state|\n|                   | - All continuous modulators/needles set to **Hidden** vis.    |\n|                   | - Complete Info View Annotations (Title &amp; Body) on all dials. |\n|                   | - Hardware Push Bank 1 configured via `[live.banks]`.         |\n+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Code Structure**| - Top-level canvas encapsulated into functional subpatchers.  |\n|                   | - All `send`, `receive`, `buffer~`, `coll`, `dict` use `---`. |\n|                   | - 100% execution determinism via `[trigger]` ordering.        |\n|                   | - Grid snapped to 8x8 (Presentation) and 15x15 (Subpatches).  |\n+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Distribution**  | - All devices **FROZEN** (Snowflake active) with dependencies.|\n|                   | - Zero console errors or un-thinned debug prints on load.     |\n|                   | - Includes $\\ge 2$ native presets (`.adv`) per device.        |\n+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **License Lock**  | - Authored 100% with native Max/MSP objects savable on the    |\n|                   |   Max for Live add-on without standalone Max 9 requirements.  |\n+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"3. Recommended Capstone Suite Blueprint: \"The Analog Production Suite\"","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Students may propose custom thematic suites or implement the standard reference blueprint:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">Analog_Production_Suite/\n├── Devices/\n│   ├── 1. Analog_Drive_Filter.amxd        &lt;-- Max Audio Effect (SVF Filter + Tape Sat)\n│   ├── 2. Euclidean_Pulse_Sequencer.amxd  &lt;-- Max MIDI Effect (Deterministic Step Seq)\n│   ├── 3. Poly_Drift_Synthesizer.amxd     &lt;-- Max Instrument (8-Voice MPE Poly Synth)\n│   └── 4. Velocity_Curve_Shaper.amxd      &lt;-- Live 12 MIDI Transformation Tool\n├── Presets/\n│   ├── Warm_Tape_Saturator.adv\n│   ├── Resonant_Acid_Lead.adv\n│   └── Ambient_Swell_Pad.adv\n├── Demo Project/\n│   └── Analog_Suite_Showcase.als          &lt;-- Fully arranged demonstration song\n└── Documentation/\n    ├── README.md                          &lt;-- Installation &amp; System Requirements\n    └── Master_QA_Audit_Report.pdf         &lt;-- Verified 24-point checklist per device</pre>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"4. Step-by-Step Capstone Execution Workflow","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Stage 1: Design Specification & Topology Planning","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["Define the musical identity and workflow purpose of your 3–5 device suite.","Draft signal flow block diagrams for each device, identifying audio/MIDI I/O boundaries, internal subpatches, and parameter lists."],"ordered":true},{"type":"heading","text":"Stage 2: Audio DSP & Logic Implementation","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["Construct the internal signal and message graphs using standard Max/MSP objects.","Implement click-free parameter smoothing (<code>[line~]</code>), feedback ceiling limits (<code>[clip~]</code>), and dynamic sample rate scaling (<code>[dspstate~]</code>).","Enforce multi-instance namespace isolation using <code>---</code> prefixes across all named buffers, tables, and wireless routing nodes."],"ordered":true},{"type":"heading","text":"Stage 3: UI Design & Parameter Hardening","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["Build clean presentation interfaces snapped to an 8x8 pixel integer grid with Ableton Sans typography.","Open the <strong>Parameters Window</strong> and audit all Long Names, types, units, modulation modes, and Initial Values.","Configure <code>[live.banks]</code> for Push hardware integration and complete all Info View Annotations.","Set all visual modulation monitors and internal targets to <strong>Hidden</strong> visibility."],"ordered":true},{"type":"heading","text":"Stage 4: Live 12 Integration & Freeze Bundling","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["If authoring a Live 12 MIDI Tool, verify dictionary schema conformity and deterministic pseudo-random seeding.","Test device active/disabled state handling via <code>[live.thisdevice]</code> outlet 2.","Declare explicit <strong>Defined Latency</strong> in the Patcher Inspector if lookahead buffers are present.","Click the Snowflake icon to <strong>Freeze</strong> each device, embedding all abstractions and scripts."],"ordered":true},{"type":"heading","text":"Stage 5: Comprehensive QA & Package Assembly","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["Execute the full <strong>24-Point Ableton Production Guidelines QA Checklist</strong> on every device.","Perform the <strong>Blind Reopen Test</strong> in an <code>.als</code> Live Set.","Perform the <strong>Offline Render Parity Test</strong> to verify phase-accurate audio exports.","Create native presets (<code>.adv</code>), compose the demonstration Live Set (<code>.als</code>), and write the master <code>README.md</code>."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"5. Final Capstone Checkpoint and Verification Rubric","blocks":[{"type":"callout","variant":"key","title":"Note","html":"[!IMPORTANT] <strong>Capstone Master Certification Criteria</strong> The Capstone Suite is certified complete when the following verification protocol passes with zero defects:"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Clean Installation Test:</strong> The complete suite is unzipped into a clean User Library directory on an independent test machine (or isolated user account).","<strong>Set Recall Verification:</strong> The <code>Analog_Suite_Showcase.als</code> demo project opens with zero missing device warnings, zero missing file dialogs, and zero red error lines in the Max Console.","<strong>Multi-Instance Integrity:</strong> Two audio effects and two MIDI effects instantiated on parallel tracks execute simultaneously with zero parameter crosstalk.","<strong>Performance Safety:</strong> Audio playback maintains smooth, glitch-free execution across tempo automation sweeps, track freezing, and offline audio rendering.","<strong>Universal Documentation:</strong> The <code>README.md</code> accurately documents all parameter controls, installation steps, and explicitly notes compatibility with Ableton Live 12 Standard (with Max for Live) / Suite without standalone Max dependencies."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"6. Source Citations","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton AG. (2023). <em>Max for Live Production Guidelines: Master QA &amp; Packaging Standards</em>, pp. 1–130. Berlin: Ableton AG.","Ableton AG. (2023). <em>Ableton Patch Code Standard: Comprehensive Engineering Reference</em>. Ableton Developer Documentation.","Cycling '74. (2024). <em>Max 9 User Guide and Reference Manual</em>. San Francisco: Cycling '74."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
